  "essentialEvidence": "Confirm the distinct final 5 EC for September 2026 entrants in Descriptive Linguistics, including the required Berber/Leti rotation or approved substitute, without counting the same Berber course twice.",
  "officialAlternative": "The active 2026–2027 BA-TWS catalogue lists the same 5 EC 5512VEBE2Y module in the required second-year group BA-TWS-2-A3-V and third-year group BA-TWS-3-A3. The exact Berber entry identifies a biennial offering. Leiden’s archived 2025–2026 prospectus lists Leti under both years and its transition section says Berber and Leti will alternate and both remain obligatory, but addresses earlier students. The exact archived Leti entry gives 5 EC and code 5513VTB05. The current and requested later catalogue module endpoints returned null for the tested Leti codes, and BA-TWS requests for 2027–2028 and 2028–2029 returned the active 2026–2027 catalogue. The published English programme regulations apply from September 2026 but do not specify the rotation, substitution or applicable semester in Article 4.2. The 2027–2028 official programme brochure still identifies Descriptive Linguistics but does not list the required course or rotation. Thus the older notice supplies a credible lead but no current distinct final 5 EC can be verified for September 2026 entrants.",
  "supportedCredits": 175
